pub fn purpose -> String =
  "When shortening a label, you may want to keep an emoji’s skin tone or a letter’s accent attached. std/text/grapheme counts and extracts user-perceived character clusters, called grapheme clusters."

pub fn units -> String =
  "A👍🏽e\\u{0301} contains three clusters: A, 👍🏽, and e with a combining accent. \\u{0301} writes the accent by its Unicode number. One Unicode code value is a scalar. The emoji modifier and accent are separate scalars, giving five scalars and twelve UTF-8 bytes."

pub fn reading -> String =
  "import gives the modules the local names graphemes and text. let names the input label. A space separates the function name from the argument label. pub effect fn main is the output entry; println prints the backtick-delimited string and a newline. ${...} inserts a calculated value and the string’s line breaks are preserved."

pub fn comparison -> String =
  "TypeScript can enumerate the same pieces using Intl.Segmenter with grapheme granularity. pieces takes each result’s segment string. Array.from(label) enumerates scalar-sized units for this well-formed text, while TextEncoder returns UTF-8 bytes. String.length gives seven UTF-16 units, a different count from three clusters."

pub fn host -> String =
  "Both versions were checked on this input. Seseragi pins its Unicode data version; Intl.Segmenter uses the host’s implementation and data. This example does not establish identical boundaries for every string across versions."

pub fn choose -> String =
  "Choose length for a count and clusters for the individual pieces. at selects one cluster and slice selects a range. byteBoundaries is for coordinating with operations that use UTF-8 byte positions."

pub fn checked -> String =
  "at returns Maybe<String>: Just with a value or Nothing for an absent position. slice returns Either: Right with a string or Left with an invalid-range reason. These are ordinary returned values. The following preview function uses match to read both slice outcomes and turn their contents into a message."

pub fn sliceReading -> String =
  "fn declares preview. start and end are Int positions, label is a String, and the final -> String specifies the returned message. Right part names its contents part; Left reason uses show to display the reason. Zero up to two contains A and 👍🏽; one up to three contains 👍🏽 and accented e. The end position itself is excluded."

pub fn repair -> String =
  "Two up to two and zero up to zero on empty text are valid empty ranges. End four, reversed bounds and a negative start return Left. length: 3 is the actual count. Changing the first invalid range from zero up to four to zero up to two produces preview: [A👍🏽]."

pub fn limits -> String =
  "These operations take work linear in UTF-8 input length; looking up a cluster is not guaranteed constant-time array access. Segmentation and slicing preserve spelling without normalization. They do not measure display width or find word and sentence boundaries."

pub fn targets -> String =
  "These pure operations are available on process and browser targets without external services. Choose normalization explicitly in std/text/unicode when you need a common spelling. std/text explains scalar operations and byte counts."
